From: Florian Klingler <klingler@ccs-labs.org>
Subject: ath: extend the ath world regulatory rules up to 5925 MHz

So that the ITS-G5 channels added to ath9k are not disabled on boards
whose EEPROM carries an Atheros world regdomain. Applied after OpenWrt's
403-world_regd_fixup.patch; macro names kept, only the upper edge moves.
Via OpenWrt-V2X 21.02.1 and MPW1412/avm-fritz3390-802.11p-otm.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/regd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/regd.c
@@ -45,9 +45,9 @@
 /* We allow IBSS on these on a case by case basis by regulatory domain */
 #define ATH_5GHZ_5150_5350	REG_RULE(5150-10, 5350+10, 80, 0, 30,\
 					 NL80211_RRF_NO_IR)
-#define ATH_5GHZ_5470_5850	REG_RULE(5470-10, 5850+10, 80, 0, 30,\
+#define ATH_5GHZ_5470_5850	REG_RULE(5470-10, 5925+10, 80, 0, 30,\
 					 NL80211_RRF_NO_IR)
-#define ATH_5GHZ_5725_5850	REG_RULE(5725-10, 5850+10, 80, 0, 30,\
+#define ATH_5GHZ_5725_5850	REG_RULE(5725-10, 5925+10, 80, 0, 30,\
 					 NL80211_RRF_NO_IR)
 
 #define ATH_2GHZ_ALL		ATH_2GHZ_CH01_11, \
